# CODEOWNERS - who must approve before a merge.
#
# This file does nothing on its own. It becomes load-bearing only when branch
# protection on `main` has "Require a review from a code owner" switched on,
# which is the state this repo expects; without that setting a CODEOWNERS file is
# decoration and reviews are optional. Verify the setting after the first push:
#
#   gh api repos/__PROJECT_OWNER__/__PROJECT_NAME__/branches/main/protection \
#     --jq '.required_pull_request_reviews.require_code_owner_review'
#
# That must print `true`. If it 404s, branch protection is not configured at all
# and `main` accepts direct pushes.
#
# A rule pointing at an account that does not exist is worse than no rule: GitHub
# silently stops requesting the review, the check stays green, and the merge
# proceeds unreviewed. Keep the handle below real.
#
# Lane owners and doc owners may add narrower rules beneath the catch-all - the
# last matching rule wins, so more specific paths go below, not above.

* @__PROJECT_OWNER__
